Dear Hiring Team,

It is with great pleasure that I submit my candidacy for the *Software Engineer* role on the Atlas Identity and Access Management team at *MongoDB*. I bring over three years of professional experience building full-stack web applications, distributed backend services, and secure production systems, along with a strong academic foundation as a Master of Science in Computer Science graduate from Pace University in New York City — the location this hybrid role is based in.

Through my experience across two engineering roles, I have led full-stack projects from technical design to delivery while owning the authentication and authorization concerns that are central to keeping a platform secure. As a Software Engineer at Sperse, I led the full-stack design and delivery of a multi-agent CRM platform using Python, LangGraph, and FastAPI that serves 10,000+ users, routing requests across 40+ specialized sub-agents with authentication and authorization enforced through tenant-aware JWT propagation and fine-grained access control. On the frontend, I built a React and TypeScript visual workflow platform (React Flow) that lets users create, run, and manage agentic swarms, backed by Temporal for durable, fault-tolerant execution — exactly the kind of full-stack ownership, from user-facing product to underlying platform, that the IAM team values. I also engineered a FastMCP server exposing 160+ backend actions with fine-grained authorization to secure multi-tenant workflows, instrumented with OpenTelemetry, and wired GitHub Actions CI/CD pipelines with trace-based evals that flag latency, accuracy, and security regressions before code ships into production.

Prior to Sperse, as a Software Engineer at Qualitest, I built backbone infrastructure in a modern compiled language that users depended on daily. I designed a cloud-agnostic, distributed Storage Service in Java and Spring Boot with PostgreSQL and Redis that handled file uploads, downloads, and deletions across AWS S3, Google Cloud Storage, and MinIO via expiring signed URLs with scoped access control — direct, hands-on experience with the multi-cloud, cloud-native design that powers MongoDB Atlas across AWS, Google Cloud, and Azure. I also optimized PostgreSQL with window functions, materialized views, and indexes to cut query latency and exposed the results through interactive React visualizations for stakeholders, and orchestrated fault-tolerant, long-running jobs with AWS Step Functions across 100K+ weekly executions. Together these roles have prepared me to collaborate across the full project lifecycle and lead the technical design, execution, and delivery of medium-sized full-stack projects on the IAM team.

I have always been passionate about intellectual honesty and big thinking, and I am excited by MongoDB's mission to empower innovators to create, transform, and disrupt industries by unleashing the power of software and data. I would love to discuss my interest in this position with your team and can be reached at #ph or #eml. Thank you for your time and consideration, I look forward to connecting!

